ture of the 80S ribosome from <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic> -tRNA-ribosome and subunit-subunit interactions</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>2001</year><volume>107</volume><fpage>373</fpage><lpage>386</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11701127</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Melese</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Xue</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The nucleolus: an organelle formed by the act of building a ribosome</article-title><source>Curr. Opin. Cell. Biol</source><year>1995</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>324</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7662360</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scheer</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Hock</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structure and function of the nucleolus</article-title><source>Curr. Opin. Cell. Biol</source><year>1999</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>390</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10395554</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fromont-Racine</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Senger</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Saveanu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fasiolo</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ribosome assembly in eukaryotes</article-title><source>Gene</source><year>2003</year><volume>313</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12957375</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13